    "_meanings": [
        ".²1 Knowledge.\n",
        ".²2 Sacred knowledge, holy learning, the scriptures of the Hindus. (Originally\n there were only three {%Vedas%}:-- {#fgveda, yajurveda#} and {#sAmaveda#},\n which are collectively called {#trayI#} ‘the sacred triad’; but a fourth,\n the {#aTarvaveda#}, was subsequently added to them, Each of the {%Vedas%}\n has two distinct parts, the {%Mantra%} or {%Samhitā%} and {%Brāhmaṇa%}.\n According to the strict orthodox faith of the Hindus the Vedas are {%a-pauruṣeya%},\n ‘not human compositions’, being supposed to have been directly revealed\n by the Supreme Being, Brahman, and are called ‘Śruti’ {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%} ‘what\n is heard or revealed’, as distinguished from ‘Smṛti’, {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%} ‘what\n is remembered or is the work of human origin’; see {#Sruti, smfti#} also;\n and the several sages, to whom the hymns of the Vedas are ascribed, are,\n therefore, called {#drazwAraH#} ‘seers’, and not {#kartAraH#} or {#srazwAraH#} ‘composers’.)\n",
        ".²3 A bundle of Kuśa grass; {#padmAkzamAlAmuta jantumArjanaM vedaM ca#}\n {#sAkzAttapa eva rUpiRO#} <ls>Bhāg. 12. 8. 34</ls>; <ls>Ms. 4. 36</ls>.\n",
        ".²4 <ab>N.</ab> of Viṣṇu.\n",
        ".²5 A part of a sacrifice ({#yajYANga#}).\n",
        ".²6 Exposition, comment, gloss.\n",
        ".²7 A metre.\n",
        ".²8 Acquisition, gain, wealth (<ab>Ved.</ab>).\n",
        ".²9 <ab>N.</ab> of the number ‘four’.\n",
        ".²10 The ritual ({#vedayatIti vedo viDiH#}); Karma-kāṇda; {#vedavAdasya#}\n {#vijYAnaM satyABAsamivAnftam#} <ls>Mb. 12. 10. 20</ls> (see Nīlakaṇthaʼs commentary).\n",
        ".²11 Smṛti literature; {#AmnAyeByaH punarvedAH prasftAH sarvatomuKAH#}\n <ls>Mb. 12. 260. 9</ls>.\n"
    ],
